t4 words: Hey, can you make our invite page look like this one I found? Plain off-white page with a solid dark green bar across the top holding our shop name in bold white, then a big bold heading underneath. Below that, one white box with a thin green border, and inside it the reward amount in huge bold red with a small line of text above and below it. Then a short numbered list of three steps, and a full-width red button at the bottom with white text, everything in a classic serif font except the button.
t5 words: Can you make our invite page look like this one I found? Bold purple bar across the top with our name in white, then a big purple heading, all on a very soft pinkish-white background. Under it, one rounded light-lilac box showing the reward amount really big and bold in blue, with a short line above and below it, then three short numbered steps underneath. Finish with one rounded bright orange button with white text, sitting on the left, not full width.
t6 words: Hey, can you make our invite page look like this screenshot? The whole page should be dark, almost black navy, with a blue strip at the top that has our name in soft yellow, and the page title in the same yellow. Under the title, put one rounded card a shade lighter than the background, with the reward amount large and bold in bright green and a short line above and below it. Then add a short numbered list of the 3 steps, and a wide yellow button with rounded corners and dark text at the bottom.
